{
  "notes": "Cinematic, E dorian, 120 BPM in a half-time feel. A lonely transmission: an FM bell beacon pinging a sparse three-pulse call (dot, dot, long) whose quarter-note echoes carry it into the dark, a nervous phase-distortion bass galloping in sixteenths under it, the player's theremin on the Smart Keys (a pure sine, mono, a long portamento and a wide vibrato; COLOR drives it into harmonics), radio static in the master (DUST), and an electro kit ticking like a clock: kick on 1, snare on 3. Dorian's major IV (A over E) is the colour of the night. Scenes: A one chord, Em, for four bars, over a heartbeat on E; B Em for two bars then IV and VII back home; C never touches the tonic (III IV v VII climbing, the suspense held); D the dorian plagal IV to i. ENERGY turns the heartbeat into the gallop, then brings the clock, then the alarm and fills. All material is original.",
